# The scenes of the spring-tests-in-slices deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# spring-tests-in-slices.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in spring-tests-in-slices.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: Spring Boot's list of versions, and its *test starters*, in the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/spring-boot/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the test dependencies
note "Step 2: the test starters for each slice, and *WireMock's standalone jar* for the courier."
show lessons/spring-tests-in-slices/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file"

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's delivery answer. A change for the printed notes gave the date a *pattern*."
show TodaysDeliveryView 8 17 "today's delivery answer" --zoom 12

## Scene 4: the weak tests
note "The *weak* tests: each one starts the whole application, and looks for words in the answer."
show WholeApplication 21 43 "the whole application, with a stand-in courier" --zoom 21,40-43
show DeliveriesApplicationTest 11 27 "the whole application, in every test" --mark 15,20,25

## Scene 5: the web slice
note "The *web* slice: only the controller and Spring's web layer, with the service stood in for."
show DeliveryWebSliceTest 17 34 "the web slice" --zoom 17,23,31-33

## Scene 6: the data slice
note "The *data* slice: only the repository and an in-memory database."
show DeliveryDataSliceTest 14 30 "the data slice" --zoom 14,27-29

## Scene 7: the JSON slice
note "The *JSON* slice: only Jackson, checking the answer field by field."
show DeliveryJsonSliceTest 16 28 "the JSON slice" --zoom 16,26-27

## Scene 8: the JSON slice names the date
note "Run the tests against today's service:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:spring-tests-in-slices:test -Pcode=today"
callout "Every whole-application test passes. Only the JSON slice looks at the date: 23/11/2026, where the description says 2026-11-23."

## Scene 9: the fixed service
note "The answer with the date as the description gives it:"
show DeliveryView 7 12 "the fixed delivery answer" --zoom 8
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:spring-tests-in-slices:test"
callout "All 9 tests pass: the slices check each layer, and one whole-application test checks the wiring."
